      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "CGI versions before 5.00 for Perl allow an infinite loop on a short request body when $DISABLE_UPLOADS is set.\n\nWhen $CGI::PUTDATA_UPLOAD or an upload hook is set, read_postdata_putdata takes a request body that is not a form submission. With $CGI::DISABLE_UPLOADS set, it discards the body by reading until Content-Length bytes have arrived. Once a body shorter than its Content-Length runs out, every read returns 0, so the loop never ends.\n\nA client can keep a server process spinning with one such request.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
